<title>UK: UK's BSG says may buy Buderus unit.</title>
<headline>UK's BSG says may buy Buderus unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British group BSG International said on Wednesday it was in talks about buying for cash German group Buderus AG's aircraft cabin outfitting business, Buderus Sell.</p>
<p>Buderus announced earlier in the day it was in talks with BSG.</p>
<p>&quot;BSG announces that it has entered into preliminary discussions with Buderus AG regarding the possible acquisition for cash of Buderus Sell GmbH,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;A further announcement will be made in due course,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>The company said Buderus Sell had a turnover of 106 million marks in the year to end-September 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
